  "body": "Add an explicit user setting that controls what 3D `Deburr` does when part of an edge is out of reach.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/deburr.rs` (`DeburrParams`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs` (`OpParams::Deburr`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, `crates/app/src/project/file.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/`\n\n## What to change\n\n1. Add an unreachable-edge policy enum (`SkipWithNote` default, `Refuse`) to `DeburrParams` and `OpParams::Deburr`.\n2. Keep `SkipWithNote` as the default. Omit edge segments that exceed cone flank slope or reach limits, and record a named note with the skipped count.\n3. Under `Refuse`, stop path generation and refuse the operation by name when any candidate segment is unreachable.\n4. Wire the policy through `sane.rs`, commands, project serialization (`serde(default)`), MCP `ParamsDto`, and UI controls (`mill2d_more_page.rs`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- `SkipWithNote` skips unreachable edge segments and attaches a named note.\n- `Refuse` rejects the operation by name when any segment fails reach, and passes when all candidate segments are reachable.\n- UI and MCP select both modes, and project round-trip tests pin the setting.\n\nPart of #1827\n",
